SweetMali: IMPORT_HOST, a program's own pages as a GPU buffer (VK_EXT_external_memory_host)

The Metal runtime (metal2vulkan) imports IOSurfaces and no-copy buffers as host memory, which needs
VK_EXT_external_memory_host in PanVK; m2vtest's import step failed without it (boot 2026-11-14). Request 0x4e
(outside panfrost's numbers) takes a page-aligned address and size in the caller's task, wires the pages
(IOMemoryDescriptor::withAddressRange + prepare), enters them into the GPU's address space and returns a handle
and GPU address like CREATE_BO. GEM_CLOSE unwires them. The pages stay cached for the processor; the program
cleans and invalidates them around the GPU's use, as the Metal frontend does for surfaces.
